## Playbook/helper findings

Findings so far: 07-done requires checking the expected node count before judging stresses, but swfea.static() only has a maximum-node guard and proceeds to solve/read results before the calling script can check its prediction. I set max_nodes to 2x the current predicted count to stop an oversized mesh before the solve; the helper still has no lower-bound pre-solve hook. The first mismatch exceeded the prediction by only 2.014x; the result was discarded. The 07-done maximum-displacement gate also comes after static() has already read arrays, so the helper does not expose a pre-stress result check. Do not treat either discarded run as a reported stress result.

