Status: partial at the 40 minute limit. Hard start 2026-11-13 19:16:41 UTC (13:16:41 CST); cutoff 19:56:41 UTC. Model: separate PETG block (40 x 30 x 20 mm, ?10.2 through bore along Y), centered ?10 x 50 mm steel pin, and two 1 mm long radius-1 mm soft pads at its ends to prevent free axial drift. The block bottom and pads? outer faces are fixed; the pin is pulled +Z by 250 N at each end. The only block/pin interface is a 0.1 mm radial-clearance no-penetration contact. Hand projected bearing stress is 500/(10 x 30) = 1.667 MPa. First 4 mm attempt stopped at the displacement gate and did not use stress. On retry, the same 24,034-node mesh passed the revised roof estimate: maximum movement 0.8244 mm at the pin cap [-5,25,10], and mean pin midspan rise 0.1241 mm. The block-hole contact-zone VM is 5.290 MPa at [-1.64,-15,16.073]. Total reaction is 500 N; bottom-block reaction is 499.866 N and pad reaction is 0.134 N, so pads carry 0.027% and the inferred contact share balances within 0.03%. The 3 mm mesh then showed `Fixture <Fixed-1> transfer failed` in a Simulation dialog on my owned PID 127048. `swfea.static()` logs and leaves unrecognized dialogs alone; I did not dismiss it or stop the job. That call did not return by the limit.

The contact proof will use 0.5 N in the working direction and a bonded twin. The detailed 05-fea clearance-fit instruction says not to reverse a load when the body starts with clearance; it prescribes the working-direction proof. The generalized line in 07-done says reverse a tiny load for contact. I follow the clearance-specific instruction, since reversing would pull the centered pin away from either wall and test its stabilizer instead of seating contact. Studies must stay below 200,000 nodes and within the 40 minute limit.

